vendor/cros-libva: cros-libva 0.0.12 (crates.io, BSD-3-Clause), with fixes: src/buffer/vp9.rs so it builds against libva 2.23+; Display::create_context never makes a context smaller than the driver's minimum surface size (cros-codecs opens every decoder with a 16x16 context, which radeonsi and nvidia-vaapi-driver refuse); Display::open_drm_display_with_driver picks the VA driver (vaSetDriverName) instead of LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME, which applies to every device; Config::query_surface_attributes has vaQuerySurfaceAttributes write the count through a mutable reference (not a cast of a shared one) and never sets the vector longer than its capacity; Display::open_drm_display_with_driver owns the display from vaGetDisplayDRM on, so a failing vaSetDriverName or vaInitialize still ends in vaTerminate. The bindings are pregenerated in src/bindings_generated.rs, so a build needs no bindgen/clang: they are the OUT_DIR/bindings.rs the crate's original build.rs (with bindgen_gen.rs and libva-wrapper.h from the crates.io package) generates from libva 2.24 headers; identical for x86_64 and aarch64. To update them, run that original build.rs against newer headers and copy the file over
vendor/re_mp4: re_mp4 0.4.0 (crates.io, MIT/Apache-2.0), unknown metadata data-atom types become Binary and odd audio track fields fall back to defaults instead of failing the whole file; Mp4::read_tracks reads the samples of only the tracks a caller picks (Mp4::read reads all of them), Mp4::into_tracks hands them over without a copy, and the samples read are at most one per byte of the file and Mp4::MAX_SAMPLES (2^23) in all, the list grown with try_reserve so that memory it can't get is an error, not an abort; the sample tables (stsc, stco/co64, stts, stsz, ctts, stss) are walked with checked lookups, so broken ones are errors instead of panics, and an mdhd duration of all ones is unknown; in fragments a sample is a sync sample when sample_is_non_sync_sample is clear (0.4.0 has it the other way round), trun version 1 composition offsets are signed (TrunBox::sample_cts is Vec<i64>), every trun starts at its own data offset and a traf without a base of its own where the one before it ends, a trun is only walked when it has fields for each sample, and the samples of fragments after samples in the moov are moved as those were (a fragment without tfdt starts where they end); BoxHeader::read, for a box inside another, refuses a size smaller than the header (0 too: it made the loop over the boxes read the same one forever), BoxHeader::read_top_level keeps 0 for a box that runs to the end of the file, meta checks the sizes of its boxes, udta may end in QuickTime's 32-bit 0, and avcC, data and emsg fields that run past the end of their box are errors
